[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   step_123: Leg-coherence decomposition of the CODE-overlap anomaly.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   Step 122 localized the weak pre-2018 declared-axis term to the 288
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   members the cohort shares with CODE (+0.216 dex, p = 0.010 under
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   independent JPL solutions).  The decisive remaining discrimination is
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   WHERE in the two-leg reconstruction the excess lives:
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   H-JOINT  the anomaly is an inter-leg coherence defect -- the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   inbound and outbound boundary asymptotes are each
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   individually consistent with the osculating solution, but
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   disagree with each other more at the cap.  This is the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   morphology a boundary interaction produces: an impulse at
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   the crossing rotates the outgoing leg relative to the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   incoming one, and the osculating fit lands between them.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   H-NOISE  the anomaly is a reconstruction floor -- in-cap members
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   have worse solutions, so either or both legs carry the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   excess and the residual elevation is a spread, not a shift.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   Both legs' absolute deviations from the osculating pericentre
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   direction (d_in, d_out), their mutual separation (drot), and the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   osculating direction itself are all in the leg record, so the full
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   three-vector geometry is recoverable: the relative azimuth phi of the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   two leg deviations about the osculating direction follows the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   spherical law of cosines,
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   cos(phi) = [cos(drot) - cos(d_in)cos(d_out)]
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   / [sin(d_in)sin(d_out)]
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   phi ~ 0 means the legs deviate coherently (a shared rotation of the
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   whole orbit); phi ~ 180 deg means the osculating direction sits
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   between two divergent asymptotes -- the twist signature of H-JOINT.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T1  leg decomposition: declared-cap gaps on resid(log d_in),
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   resid(log d_out) and resid(log drot) for the CODE-overlap and
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   non-overlap members.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T2  twist coherence: cos(phi) in-cap vs out-of-cap on the overlap
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   (well-conditioned members only); anti-aligned fraction
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   (cos(phi) < -0.5); non-overlap control.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T3  noise-floor rejection: per-object data quality (arc, nobs)
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   in-cap vs out-of-cap on the overlap; residual dispersion
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   (MAD ratio, Levene); mean-vs-median shift decomposition.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T4  per-comet cross-fitter concordance: JPL-solution resid vs
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   CODE-solution resid on matched designations -- the carrier-level
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   agreement between the two fitters, with the attenuation bound
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   that a uniform cap shift on independent fitter noise predicts.
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T5  class-constraint gradient: the cap gap ordered by CODE quality
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   class on the overlap -- the absorption-gradient signature of a
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   real discrepancy (tighter fits absorb more of it).
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   T6  bound-solution subset: the overlap gap on JPL-bound (e<1)
[2026-09-21 15:14:06 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 123]   members only.
